# Tier 1 credentials.
#
# Set these as GitHub repository secrets — Settings -> Secrets and variables ->
# Actions — NOT in a local file. The workflows read them from the Actions
# environment; nothing in this repo reads a local .env.
#
# This file exists to document what the pipeline needs, not to be filled in.
#
#   CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN   Auth for the cloud coding agent that processes
#                             ingestion issues. Expires. When it does, runs fail
#                             instantly with zero model usage — see
#                             TROUBLESHOOTING.md, which explains why that
#                             signature is distinctive.
#
#   GH_PERSONAL_TOKEN         GitHub PAT, scopes: repo, workflow. Opens the
#                             ingestion issue and the PR. Also expires, and
#                             fails differently: issues stop being created at
#                             all, with nothing useful in the Actions log.
#
# Both expire. Put their expiry dates in a calendar a month ahead — the pipeline
# stops silently, and files just accumulate in intake/inbox/ looking unprocessed.
#
# At Tier 0 none of this applies and the install skill deletes this file.
#
# Building the capture extension (docs/automated-capture.md) will add provider
# credentials of its own. Those belong in that provider's or job runner's own
# secret store, never here.
